it's officially monsoon season we know  during a thunderstorm rain can  fall very quickly that means the threat  of flash flooding bianca holman is in  henderson to show us  what's keeping your family safe  we're here at the pitman north detention  basin in henderson  this basin protects businesses roads and  thousands of homes across henderson and  in the southern highlands neighborhood  flash floods are dangerous and deadly so  local agencies are trying to raise  awareness to prevent deaths and injuries  flood channels flow into this large  basin holding water trash  and dirt the basin is built to for a  potential 100 year flood and even though  there's only a one percent chance of it  happening the regional flood control  district  is prepared no human interaction is  needed for this structure  to operate no need for a gate or switch  it's here  working all the time 24 7 365 days a  week it doesn't matter if it starts  raining at 2 am in the morning this  basin will be here  to protect the properties downstream so  i as the general manager of a flight  control district i really appreciate the  fact that i sleep better at night  knowing that these facilities are in  place  and protecting the community there are  plans to help protect older areas across  the valley  the national weather service and fire  department want to remind everyone to  use  caution when driving in the rain matter  of fact as little as six inches can  cause your vehicle to swerve  and 12 inches can cause your vehicle to  float  they also want to remind people if you  see a pool of water turn around don't  drown  and never play in the water flood  channels bianca holman 8 news now
 

